> Normality with specified or fitted parameters

Shapiro–Wilk and Shapiro–Francia test composite normality with different
order-statistic weights. Shapiro–Wilk uses an exact tail for three observations
and Royston's approximation for larger supported samples. The one-sample
Kolmogorov–Smirnov test in the table uses a normal distribution with mean zero
and standard deviation one specified in advance. If the normal mean and variance
are estimated from the same data, use Lilliefors calibration. The Lilliefors
implementation refits both quantities for each standard-normal simulation,
using a seeded plus-one Monte Carlo p-value.

```{cpp, id=shape-tests, cache=yes, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/stats/additional_tests.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/ks_test.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/normality_test.hpp>
#include <print>
#include <string_view>
#include <vector>

namespace s = datamunge::stats;

int main() {
    const std::vector<double> sample{-1.5, -.8, -.3, -.1, .2, .4, .7, 1.7, 2.3};
    const auto row = [](std::string_view test, std::string_view api, const s::HypothesisTestResult& result) {
        std::println("| {} | `{}` | {:.7g} | {:.7g} |", test, api, result.statistic, result.p_value);
    };
    std::println("| Test | Native entry point | Statistic | p-value |\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |");
    row("Shapiro–Wilk", "shapiro_wilk_test", s::shapiro_wilk_test(sample));
    row("Kolmogorov–Smirnov", "ks_test_one_sample_normal", s::ks_test_one_sample_normal(sample, 0, 1));
    row("Shapiro–Francia", "shapiro_francia_test", s::shapiro_francia_test(sample));
    row("Lilliefors", "lilliefors_test", s::lilliefors_test(sample, 9999, 42));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Test | Native entry point | Statistic | p-value |
| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |
| Shapiro–Wilk | `shapiro_wilk_test` | 0.9763523 | 0.9429426 |
| Kolmogorov–Smirnov | `ks_test_one_sample_normal` | 0.1776568 | 0.9115581 |
| Shapiro–Francia | `shapiro_francia_test` | 0.9761857 | 0.9556392 |
| Lilliefors | `lilliefors_test` | 0.1413696 | 0.8633 |
// result_end

